<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Push notifications (FCM/APNs). Must match the provisioning profile's
	     environment. Every CI build is DISTRIBUTION-signed — the ad-hoc
	     `zoonze-shop-adhoc` profile (build-on-push) and the TestFlight/App Store
	     profiles all carry `aps-environment=production` (get-task-allow=false).
	     A `development` value on a distribution-signed build makes
	     `registerForRemoteNotifications` fail, so APNs hands over no device token
	     (the FCM token then stays null). Use `production`. (Only a local Xcode
	     debug run with a *development* profile would need `development`.) -->
	<!-- APPLE PAY — intentionally NOT declared yet.
	     The wallet code is in place (PaymentChannel.swift, ApplePaySession.swift)
	     but the merchant entitlement is deliberately absent until the external
	     setup is done, because declaring it here without regenerating the
	     provisioning profiles produces a build that fails to install locally and
	     an Apple Pay sheet that cannot be presented on device.

	     To enable, IN THIS ORDER:
	       1. Apple Developer portal -> Identifiers -> Merchant IDs: create
	          merchant.com.zoonze.shop (confirm the exact string with Network
	          International first — it must match what they register).
	       2. Get the Apple Pay payment-processing CSR from N-Genius, upload it
	          against the merchant id, return the certificate to them. Without
	          this the sheet completes but authorisation always fails, because
	          N-Genius cannot decrypt the PKPaymentToken.
	       3. App ID com.zoonze.shop -> enable "Apple Pay Payment Processing" and
	          associate the merchant id.
	       4. REGENERATE BOTH ios/signing/*.mobileprovision (an existing profile
	          never picks up a new capability). Keep the same filenames; keep the
	          ad-hoc profile's device UDIDs; keep the App Store profile free of a
	          ProvisionedDevices list — tool/ios_*_build.sh picks the profile
	          solely on that key.
	       5. Add the key here, and set APPLE_PAY_MERCHANT_ID in config/*.json to
	          the same string.

	     Note CI archives UNSIGNED and re-signs with the PROFILE's entitlements
	     (tool/ios_*_build.sh step 5d), so this file governs local Xcode builds
	     only — the profile is what actually ships. Those scripts assert the two
	     stay in sync once the key is added here.

	<key>com.apple.developer.in-app-payments</key>
	<array>
		<string>merchant.com.zoonze.shop</string>
	</array>
	-->

	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>production</string>
</dict>
</plist>
